    fix(optics): dielectric_metal→dielectric_dielectric enabling TIR on bar skin surface
    
    exec21-optfix: replaces dielectric_metal (R=0.98, no TIR) with dielectric_dielectric
    (polished, unified) on the bar LogicalSkinSurface. This enables TIR for photons at
    angles > arcsin(1/1.58)=39.3° relative to the bar surface normal, dramatically
    improving light collection at END SiPMs from ~0.37 PE (no TIR) to O(100) PE.
    
    Root cause identified in EXEC_21 D4: with 164 average bounces to reach END face,
    dielectric_metal with R=0.98 gives only 0.98^164=3.6% survival, then additional
    ABSLENGTH attenuation over ~328 cm path → 0.04 PE expected (observed: 0.37 PE).
    Even R=1.0 metallic gives only 1.2 PE. TIR is the only physical fix.
    
    Non-TIR photons now escape the bar (no Mylar recovery); a follow-up commit
    should add explicit Mylar wrapping volume to recover non-TIR photons.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/Materials.cc b/src/Materials.cc
